{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"change in estimate criterion change in estimate criterion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","fileName":"Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Change-in-Estimate Criterion","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regression Model Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"change in estimate criterion change in estimate criterion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","fileName":"Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Change-in-Estimate Criterion","heading":"Change-in-Estimate Criterion","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A change-in-estimate criterion retains a candidate confounder when adding it changes the exposure coefficient by more than a chosen relative amount, often ten percent. It focuses on distortion of the target association rather than the confounder's own p-value.\n\nThe threshold is a practical rule, not a statistical test for confounding. Its result depends on the coefficient scale and the current model, so substantive knowledge and the broader selection strategy still govern the decision.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regression Model Development","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Change-in-Estimate Criterion.md::